+# Equipment observation and process history
+
+[中文](README.zh-CN.md) · [Integration contract](../../../contracts/published/http-api/equipment-observation-v1/README.md) · [r7 specification](../../../plans/ARCH-OBS-001-configuration-driven-equipment-monitoring/spec.md#9-r7-首版业务闭环)
+
+The manifest registers machine ingest, business reads, administrator configuration, seven separate business tables and two read permissions. It depends on the read-only task evidence exported by `plc_facts`. The private profile is default-off and loaded from outside the repository; it owns credential digests, device scopes, history whitelists and per-device/group staleness thresholds. Alembic explicitly migrates the schema; startup and registration neither create tables nor seed data. Existing PLC facts and typed APIs keep their own permissions and contracts. `equipment_latest_snapshots` overwrites; `monitor_history_samples` appends. Each target has durable receipts and independent retries, and receipts retain task-point evidence. The Web resolves metric keys, labels and units from configuration; slot numbers are not the external API.
